Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:31:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Take a pairing file put in place after the first one

The Cartouche Installer, and Cartouche's own setup, put a pairing file in
place as ALTPairingFile.mobiledevicepairing, the name iloader uses for a
LiveContainer+SideStore. SideStore moves such a file to its own names,
PairingFile_RemoteRP.plist and PairingFile_Lockdown.plist, once, at its
first launch (MaintenanceManager.migratePairingFiles, maintenance pass 7),
and fetchPairingFile reads those before the legacy name ever after. So a
pairing file put in place again, which Cartouche asks for when the iPhone
refuses the one it has, was never read: SideStore went on with the one it
had moved.

fetchPairingFile now takes a file put in place under the legacy name first:
each kind it holds is written over SideStore's own file of that kind, the
kind it does not hold is removed, the protocol it is read with is recorded
as importPairingFile does, and the file goes, as the migration does. A file
that is not a pairing file stays where it is, read last, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MzPJouaxDEHiaAYJRW7jTY
---
 .../Core/Pairing/PairingFileManager.swift     | 33 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/SideStore/Core/Pairing/PairingFileManager.swift b/SideStore/Core/Pairing/PairingFileManager.swift
index b0c10da..41f7330 100644
--- a/SideStore/Core/Pairing/PairingFileManager.swift
+++ b/SideStore/Core/Pairing/PairingFileManager.swift
@@ -145,7 +145,40 @@ final class PairingFileManager: NSObject {
         return String(data: try! PropertyListSerialization.data(fromPropertyList: ansDict, format: .xml, options: 0), encoding: .utf8)!
     }
 
+    /// Cartouche: a pairing file put in place under the legacy name, by the
+    /// Cartouche Installer or Cartouche's own setup, replaces the ones
+    /// SideStore keeps under its own names. SideStore moves such a file to
+    /// its own names once, at its first launch
+    /// (MaintenanceManager.migratePairingFiles), and reads those first ever
+    /// after: a pairing file put in place again, to replace one the iPhone
+    /// refuses, was never read. Each kind the file holds is written first,
+    /// over the file before, so that a read meanwhile finds one or the other.
+    /// Needs proper testing on an iPhone whose pairing file was replaced.
+    nonisolated func adoptPlacedPairingFile() {
+        let fm = FileManager.default
+        let placedURL = pairingFileURL(for: .unknown)
+        guard let contents = try? String(contentsOf: placedURL), !contents.isEmpty else { return }
+        let kinds: [PairingProtocol] = [.rppairing, .lockdown].filter { (try? parse(content: contents, preferred: $0)) != nil }
+        // Not a pairing file SideStore reads: it stays, read last, as before.
+        guard let active = kinds.first else { return }
+        do {
+            for mode in kinds {
+                try contents.write(to: pairingFileURL(for: mode), atomically: true, encoding: .utf8)
+            }
+        } catch {
+            debugLog("[PairingFile] Could not take the pairing file put in place: \(error)")
+            return
+        }
+        for mode in [PairingProtocol.rppairing, .lockdown] where !kinds.contains(mode) {
+            try? fm.removeItem(at: pairingFileURL(for: mode))
+        }
+        persistedActiveProtocol = active
+        try? fm.removeItem(at: placedURL)
+        debugLog("[PairingFile] Took the pairing file put in place: \(kinds.map(\.rawValue))")
+    }
+
     nonisolated func fetchPairingFile(preferred: PairingProtocol? = nil) -> String? {
+        adoptPlacedPairingFile()
         let targetPreferred = preferred ?? preferredProtocol
         if let targetPreferred {
             if let contents = fetchPairingFile(for: targetPreferred) {
